    "patch": "@@ -47,3 +47,7 @@ loops.cmd\n /*.cnc\n /*.png\n /*.mch\n+\n+# Python bytecode from the site tests and tools (#4386): never tracked.\n+__pycache__/\n+*.pyc"
  },
  {
    "sha": "32a452a7043f190c9119a446ab03a53e1de03132",
    "filename": "docs/decisions/4386-pycache-ignore.md",
    "status": "added",
    "additions": 17,
    "deletions": 0,
    "changes": 17,
    "blob_url": "https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/8e27d2e8eb4db3e788815717b6c8a04849cb2b50/docs%2Fdecisions%2F4386-pycache-ignore.md",
    "raw_url": "https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/raw/8e27d2e8eb4db3e788815717b6c8a04849cb2b50/docs%2Fdecisions%2F4386-pycache-ignore.md",
    "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/contents/docs%2Fdecisions%2F4386-pycache-ignore.md?ref=8e27d2e8eb4db3e788815717b6c8a04849cb2b50",
    "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+## #4386 - Python bytecode is never tracked\n+\n+**What was decided.** The 17 tracked `.pyc` blobs under\n+`site/tests/__pycache__/` and `site/tools/__pycache__/` are removed from the\n+index, and `.gitignore` gets the rules `__pycache__/` and `*.pyc` for the\n+whole tree.\n+\n+**Why.** The blobs came in with the laser stack's icons commit\n+(`1d174e09c`). Each run of the site tests rewrites them, so a worktree that\n+ran the tests showed changed tracked files, and the blobs were the only\n+conflicts of #4288. A rule for the whole tree also covers a new Python\n+folder.\n+\n+**Considered and dropped.** A rule only for `site/`: other folders can get\n+Python tools later, and no tracked file anywhere needs bytecode.\n+\n+**Cost to change later.** Two lines of `.gitignore`."
  },
